{title: Where I Am}
{subtitle: John 12:26}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 75}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] [C6] | [Bb] [F/A] | [Gm] | [Asus4] [A] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[A][Dm]The hour has come for the [Am/C]Son of Man [Bb]to [C]be [F]glorified
A [Dm]grain of wheat falls in[Am/C]to the earth and [Bb]dies
[Gm]It remains a[Dm]lone if it does not [C]break
But [Bb]if it dies, it [A]bears much fruit in the [Dm]end
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
Who[Bb]ever loves his life [C]loses it in this [Dm]world
Who[Bb]ever hates his life [C]keeps it for eternal [Dm]life
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]If any[F]one serves [C]me, he [Dm]must follow [Bb]me
Where [F]I am, [C]there my servant [Dm]will be al[Bb]so
The Fa[F]ther will honor [C]him who serves me [Dm]here
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
My soul is troubled now, [C]what shall I say
[Bb]Father, save me from this [A]hour of pain
[Bb]No, for [C]this purpose I came to [Dm]this hour
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]If any[F]one serves [C]me, he [Dm]must follow [Bb]me
Where [F]I am, [C]there my servant [Dm]will be al[Bb]so
The Fa[F]ther will honor [C]him who serves me [Dm][Bb]here
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Father, glori[C]fy your name in this mo[Bb]ment
A voice came from heaven, [C]I have glorified [Bb]it
And I will [C]glorify [Dm]it again, said [Bb]the voice
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[F]Where I am, [C]there my servant [Dm]will [Bb][F][C][Dm][Bb][F][C]be
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
